 Run: `multiplayer/run-test.sh [path/to/openmw]`, then load a save. Watch `openmw.log` for `[mp]` lines.
 Protocol: one JSON object per line, `{"t":"state","name","cell","pos":[x,y,z],"yaw"}`; the server adds `id`.
+
+## Shared world state (stage 3)
+`mod/scripts/mp/worldsync.lua` syncs, through the relay's replayed change log:
+- game time (the lowest-id client is "host" and publishes it every 5 s),
+- non-teleport doors (open/close), picked-up items, and items dropped at runtime.
+Objects from content files are addressed as `<file>:<index>` (load-order independent); runtime drops as `<senderId>/<localId>`.
+Changes for objects that are not loaded yet are applied when the object becomes active.
+Not synced yet: container contents, NPC/creature deaths and combat, quests/globals, weather, locks.
+Remote-player stand-ins can't be activated (no dialogue/pickpocket).
